# ── Real research data ──
# NHAMCS public-use files are ~80 MB and are redistributed by the CDC, not by
# this repository. The loader downloads them on demand:
#     python -m data.real.nhamcs_loader --download 2022
# The record layouts and parse validation are in version control; the raw
# survey files are not.
# The compressed public-use files ARE tracked: 3.7 MB for both years, against
# 73 MB extracted. They are US federal public-domain data, freely
# redistributable, and shipping them is what lets someone clone this
# repository and run it without a download step. The loader extracts them
# automatically on first use.
data/real/ed20*/
data/real/*.pdf

# ── Trained artefacts ──
# The bundle IS tracked. It is 8.3 MB, and it is what makes `streamlit run
# app.py` work on a fresh clone: without it the application cannot start, and
# regenerating it means running the full training job first. Reproducible from
# source at any time with `python -m scripts.train_model`.

# ── Runtime ──
logs/*.jsonl
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.DS_Store
.venv/
venv/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ── Pitch and commercial material — not part of the code submission ──
# These stay in the working folder because they are the actual competition
# deliverables, submitted through the AIC portal. This repository is scoped to
# the code and the running prototype, so they are deliberately not published.
business-proposal.md
PatientTriage-ai_Detailed-Business-Proposal.pdf
presentation.md
presentation/

# ── Third-party documents ──
# Accenture's challenge brief. Theirs to distribute, not ours.
Problem_Statement.pdf
